1
00:00:31,364 --> 00:00:32,657
How in the world…

2
00:00:39,039 --> 00:00:42,542
SPIDER STAFFING AGENCY

3
00:00:43,209 --> 00:00:44,419
Great work.

4
00:00:44,919 --> 00:00:46,337
Here. Your pay.

5
00:00:48,465 --> 00:00:51,009
Labor is such a fascinating thing.

6
00:00:52,552 --> 00:00:54,846
While doing it,
you have all these mixed feelings

7
00:00:54,929 --> 00:00:57,515
and feel like you're going to die.

8
00:00:58,308 --> 00:01:02,020
But the moment you get paid,
you forget all about it.

9
00:01:04,022 --> 00:01:04,939
What do you think?

10
00:01:05,774 --> 00:01:06,858
Sweet, isn't it?

11
00:01:10,987 --> 00:01:12,155
So

12
00:01:13,031 --> 00:01:14,616
about what happened last night…

13
00:01:14,699 --> 00:01:18,578
We don't know
what exactly happens at the workplace.

14
00:01:18,661 --> 00:01:21,039
We just introduce and connect people.

15
00:01:21,122 --> 00:01:23,208
How does that connection work exactly?

16
00:01:25,335 --> 00:01:26,544
That's a trade secret.

17
00:01:26,628 --> 00:01:29,422
You're really not going to tell me?
I almost died last night.

18
00:01:29,506 --> 00:01:32,383
This is something else entirely.
What I saw last night…

19
00:01:34,719 --> 00:01:35,929
What was all of that?

20
00:01:36,429 --> 00:01:37,680
Was I imagining things?

21
00:01:41,184 --> 00:01:43,770
If you must know,

22
00:01:45,021 --> 00:01:46,898
you could say the world we live in

23
00:01:47,607 --> 00:01:49,526
looks like this.

24
00:01:55,073 --> 00:01:56,282
We live on this side.

25
00:01:57,700 --> 00:01:58,993
Then the other side?

26
00:02:00,495 --> 00:02:02,914
The world we live in is yang.

27
00:02:03,998 --> 00:02:05,792
The other is yin.

28
00:02:07,502 --> 00:02:10,964
Yin and yang cannot see each other…

29
00:02:15,009 --> 00:02:16,344
<i>but between them,</i>

30
00:02:17,095 --> 00:02:18,805
<i>there must exist a boundary.</i>

31
00:02:20,348 --> 00:02:22,517
<i>When that boundary becomes unstable,</i>

32
00:02:23,017 --> 00:02:25,645
<i>the energy from the other world invades,</i>

33
00:02:26,479 --> 00:02:28,857
<i>and strange things start to happen.</i>

34
00:02:30,608 --> 00:02:33,570
<i>When the energy</i>
<i>from the other world invades,</i>

35
00:02:34,154 --> 00:02:39,159
<i>we place a strong yang energy</i>
<i>to suppress that yin energy.</i>

36
00:02:39,742 --> 00:02:41,411
<i>That's labor.</i>

37
00:02:42,912 --> 00:02:47,750
Because there's no stronger yang energy
than the struggle to make a living.

38
00:02:48,293 --> 00:02:49,544
Do you understand now?

39
00:02:51,296 --> 00:02:55,633
So what kind of work would you like to do?

40
00:02:58,845 --> 00:03:01,097
Wait, I can choose?

41
00:03:01,181 --> 00:03:02,849
This is a staffing agency.

42
00:03:02,932 --> 00:03:05,685
We connect you to jobs
that fit your needs.

43
00:03:05,768 --> 00:03:06,769
Then,

44
00:03:07,437 --> 00:03:09,814
is there a job that I can do
during the day?

45
00:03:09,898 --> 00:03:11,649
Something during the day…

46
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:13,568
One that doesn't require an all-nighter

47
00:03:13,651 --> 00:03:16,487
and that I can do in an open space
with a clear head.

48
00:03:16,571 --> 00:03:18,907
An open space…

49
00:03:25,038 --> 00:03:27,999
KD PHARMACEUTICAL, EVENT MANAGER
100 TIMES THE DAILY WAGE, 4 P.M. - 10 P.M.

50
00:03:28,124 --> 00:03:29,375
One hundred times!

51
00:03:29,959 --> 00:03:33,504
Oh, I forgot to tell you.

52
00:03:34,005 --> 00:03:38,885
If you complete a part-time job,
your daily wage is at least doubled.

53
00:03:44,349 --> 00:03:48,102
But what do I need to do
for this manager job?

54
00:03:49,938 --> 00:03:51,231
You'd be driving.

55
00:03:52,982 --> 00:03:55,026
All I have to do is drive?

56
00:03:55,109 --> 00:03:56,236
That's right.

57
00:03:56,736 --> 00:03:59,864
The person you'll be with
is an event specialist.

58
00:04:00,990 --> 00:04:04,744
Just drive them to the event venue
without any issues.

59
00:04:09,707 --> 00:04:11,542
Just get through the day.

60
00:04:12,043 --> 00:04:13,711
You need to make money.

61
00:04:26,307 --> 00:04:28,351
ACCEPT

62
00:04:42,699 --> 00:04:44,158
Where were you just now?

63
00:04:46,786 --> 00:04:48,830
Fortune-telling and tarot?

64
00:04:50,331 --> 00:04:51,165
Excuse me?

65
00:04:51,916 --> 00:04:54,043
That was too unexpected, wasn't it?

66
00:04:54,627 --> 00:04:57,422
I'm investigating the staffing agency
in this building.

67
00:04:57,505 --> 00:04:59,090
Do you have a moment?

68
00:05:01,259 --> 00:05:04,846
Now that I got a closer look, your face

69
00:05:05,888 --> 00:05:07,473
looks really dull and tired.

70
00:05:07,974 --> 00:05:09,684
Did you have a brutal night shift?

71
00:05:09,767 --> 00:05:12,979
What… What in the world are you doing?

72
00:05:15,023 --> 00:05:16,357
Let's have a cup of tea.

73
00:05:16,441 --> 00:05:18,735
Give me ten, no,
just five minutes of your time.

74
00:05:18,818 --> 00:05:21,279
Just in case you forgot.

75
00:05:21,863 --> 00:05:24,907
I have some questions
about Spider Staffing Agency.

76
00:05:25,533 --> 00:05:27,535
<i>If you disclose details about these jobs…</i>

77
00:05:27,618 --> 00:05:28,995
My name is Eum Yeon-joo.

78
00:05:30,371 --> 00:05:32,915
…you incur a penalty fee.
You know that, right?

79
00:05:34,917 --> 00:05:35,960
Here's--

80
00:05:36,794 --> 00:05:37,962
No, I'm sorry.

81
00:06:42,068 --> 00:06:45,780
DEAD-END JOB

82
00:06:46,948 --> 00:06:49,909
EPISODE 2
A JOURNEY WITH A PIERROT

83
00:06:56,958 --> 00:06:58,793
Mom, I'm home!

84
00:06:58,876 --> 00:07:01,254
What do we have here?

85
00:07:01,337 --> 00:07:02,505
It's a two-plus grade.

86
00:07:03,047 --> 00:07:03,881
Beef?

87
00:07:03,965 --> 00:07:04,799
Yeah.

88
00:07:08,761 --> 00:07:09,762
A million won.

89
00:07:10,471 --> 00:07:11,764
Look at you.

90
00:07:12,807 --> 00:07:15,435
- Did you get a job?
- Just part-time.

91
00:07:16,018 --> 00:07:17,854
Part-time. I see.

92
00:07:18,729 --> 00:07:21,232
Sorry. I should get a real job soon,
but it's not easy.

93
00:07:21,732 --> 00:07:23,401
No need to rush.

94
00:07:24,277 --> 00:07:27,822
While you're at it, take your time
and find something you're good at.

95
00:07:27,905 --> 00:07:29,240
That's the fastest way.

96
00:07:29,991 --> 00:07:31,325
Look at your father.

97
00:07:31,826 --> 00:07:35,163
He dabbled in everything,
but maybe he couldn't handle it.

98
00:07:35,663 --> 00:07:37,582
He suddenly disappeared.

99
00:07:47,717 --> 00:07:48,843
Alrighty.

100
00:07:57,226 --> 00:07:58,186
Hey, son.

101
00:07:58,686 --> 00:08:00,980
What do you think,
watching your dad practice?

102
00:08:01,481 --> 00:08:02,315
Well…

103
00:08:02,398 --> 00:08:03,691
<i>He's cool.</i>

104
00:08:03,774 --> 00:08:04,609
A FATHER'S MIRACLE

105
00:08:04,734 --> 00:08:07,278
<i>Do you want to be like your dad</i>
<i>when you grow up?</i>

106
00:08:07,778 --> 00:08:10,114
<i>Yes! I want to be like my dad.</i>

107
00:08:11,449 --> 00:08:12,283
<i>Oh, come on.</i>

108
00:08:12,783 --> 00:08:14,827
<i>You should live differently.</i>

109
00:08:14,911 --> 00:08:15,912
<i>Differently?</i>

110
00:08:16,454 --> 00:08:20,666
<i>Live the exact opposite of me, kid.</i>

111
00:08:20,750 --> 00:08:23,044
<i>Make lots and lots of money,</i>

112
00:08:23,127 --> 00:08:25,463
<i>and take good care of your family.</i>

113
00:08:28,633 --> 00:08:29,842
My God!

114
00:08:30,593 --> 00:08:32,220
<i>You're so funny, sir.</i>

115
00:08:32,303 --> 00:08:33,346
It's your sister.

116
00:08:33,846 --> 00:08:35,431
- What are you doing?
- <i>But I mean it.</i>

117
00:08:35,973 --> 00:08:38,935
Damn it! I told you
not to break into my room!

118
00:08:39,018 --> 00:08:39,852
You…

119
00:08:40,561 --> 00:08:41,729
Why are you here?

120
00:08:41,812 --> 00:08:43,981
What happened here? Did someone hit you?

121
00:08:44,065 --> 00:08:45,107
- Why do you care?
- Who?

122
00:08:45,191 --> 00:08:47,109
Why the hell are you here?

123
00:08:47,193 --> 00:08:48,194
Damn it.

124
00:08:48,694 --> 00:08:50,696
Are you watching that again?

125
00:08:51,197 --> 00:08:52,323
Do you miss your daddy?

126
00:08:52,406 --> 00:08:55,159
Are you crazy?
I just needed to check something.

127
00:08:55,243 --> 00:08:57,620
Who cares about a dad
who abandoned his family?

128
00:08:58,788 --> 00:09:00,623
Throw this trash out.

129
00:09:00,706 --> 00:09:01,791
Don't put it back!

130
00:09:01,874 --> 00:09:02,917
Seriously.

131
00:09:03,417 --> 00:09:05,086
Why'd you come? To piss me off?

132
00:09:07,838 --> 00:09:09,006
Give me some money.

133
00:09:10,007 --> 00:09:11,801
See? You did come to piss me off.

134
00:09:12,385 --> 00:09:14,345
I have a job interview tomorrow.

135
00:09:14,428 --> 00:09:16,180
I can't go looking like this.

136
00:09:16,264 --> 00:09:19,100
I should at least wear something nice.

137
00:09:19,183 --> 00:09:20,101
Just go like that.

138
00:09:20,184 --> 00:09:23,479
You know,
going to those things in new clothes

139
00:09:23,563 --> 00:09:24,814
brings bad luck.

140
00:09:26,566 --> 00:09:30,987
You should have the money Mom lent you
to get a <i>jeonse </i>lease.

141
00:09:32,738 --> 00:09:36,075
Why would I give that to you?
Mom gave it to me to get a place.

142
00:09:36,158 --> 00:09:39,495
God, she saved up that money
working herself to the bone,

143
00:09:39,579 --> 00:09:41,872
anxiously waiting
and trusting her only son--

144
00:09:41,956 --> 00:09:45,334
Are you implying that I blew that money?

145
00:09:47,962 --> 00:09:50,673
Just place a few bills here nicely
before I tell Mom.

146
00:09:51,882 --> 00:09:53,634
Tell her what?

147
00:09:53,718 --> 00:09:56,178
That you invested in stocks, you moron.

148
00:09:58,931 --> 00:10:00,057
Is it obvious?

149
00:10:00,141 --> 00:10:01,642
Like it isn't. Seriously.

150
00:10:02,602 --> 00:10:03,644
How much did you lose?

151
00:10:04,770 --> 00:10:06,647
What? Are you too embarrassed to say?

152
00:10:07,148 --> 00:10:07,982
Half of it?

153
00:10:10,318 --> 00:10:11,319
70%?

154
00:10:15,948 --> 00:10:16,866
All of it?

155
00:10:17,617 --> 00:10:18,534
Seriously?

156
00:10:18,618 --> 00:10:20,870
I'm in the middle of making it back.

157
00:10:21,454 --> 00:10:22,830
Are you out of your mind?

158
00:10:22,913 --> 00:10:25,124
Sleep here tonight
and go to your interview.

159
00:10:25,207 --> 00:10:27,585
I'll give you money when I get back.

160
00:10:27,668 --> 00:10:29,503
- Where are you going?
- I got a thing.

161
00:10:30,212 --> 00:10:33,007
- Did you get a part-time gig?
- I said I got a thing.

162
00:10:33,090 --> 00:10:35,509
You better not do anything weird
or get into fights!

163
00:10:35,593 --> 00:10:37,053
- It's not like that!
- Damn it.

164
00:10:38,596 --> 00:10:40,014
Like hell it isn't.

165
00:10:40,514 --> 00:10:42,266
Your face tells me something's up.

166
00:11:01,661 --> 00:11:03,329
"KD Pharmaceutical"?

167
00:11:05,039 --> 00:11:06,332
Is this the right place?

168
00:11:06,415 --> 00:11:11,879
KD PHARMACEUTICAL, EVENT MANAGER
100 TIMES THE DAILY WAGE, 4 P.M. - 10 P.M.

169
00:11:20,137 --> 00:11:22,390
Damn it. First a rat and now a pig?

170
00:11:35,569 --> 00:11:36,445
Hello.

171
00:11:36,946 --> 00:11:38,406
You came right on the dot?

172
00:11:38,489 --> 00:11:41,492
This is ridiculous.

173
00:11:42,660 --> 00:11:44,453
- Who do you think you are?
- Sorry?

174
00:11:45,079 --> 00:11:48,249
I said, who do you think you are?

175
00:11:50,876 --> 00:11:53,963
My name is Byeon Hyeok-jun.

176
00:11:54,046 --> 00:11:55,131
I'm 30 years old and--

177
00:11:55,214 --> 00:11:57,174
Who the hell asked you
to introduce yourself?

178
00:11:58,342 --> 00:12:00,594
Your client is stuck here waiting for you,

179
00:12:00,678 --> 00:12:02,138
and you part-timers are late?

180
00:12:02,221 --> 00:12:04,765
I'm sorry. I got the call a bit late, so--

181
00:12:04,849 --> 00:12:08,185
Didn't your damn company tell you
that Mr. Jo has a nasty temper?

182
00:12:10,146 --> 00:12:11,522
No, it didn't.

183
00:12:18,654 --> 00:12:19,947
Hurry up.

184
00:12:23,868 --> 00:12:26,579
It seems you've never had a proper job,
so let me teach you.

185
00:12:27,079 --> 00:12:29,331
I bet you got low grades. Which college?

186
00:12:29,999 --> 00:12:32,501
- I just went to a regional one--
- This is a KOSPI-listed company.

187
00:12:32,585 --> 00:12:35,045
I got better grades
and went to a university in Seoul.

188
00:12:35,880 --> 00:12:39,842
And today, we're attending
a university hospital department offsite.

189
00:12:39,925 --> 00:12:42,219
Those bastards
were the top students in Korea.

190
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:44,054
Are you getting the drift?

191
00:12:46,599 --> 00:12:48,392
So they're impressive…

192
00:12:50,352 --> 00:12:51,562
people,

193
00:12:52,104 --> 00:12:53,397
right? Like me.

194
00:12:55,024 --> 00:12:57,526
Like you? Like hell they are.

195
00:12:57,610 --> 00:13:01,614
The pecking order in Korea
is decided by who has brains, got it?

196
00:13:01,697 --> 00:13:05,201
They're at the top, I'm in the middle,
and you're at the bottom!

197
00:13:05,284 --> 00:13:07,036
Get it? The bottom!

198
00:13:08,162 --> 00:13:09,538
The bottom.

199
00:13:11,999 --> 00:13:14,376
Go get me a coffee
from the snack bar, you punk.

200
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:17,463
No wonder he's still working
part-time jobs.

201
00:13:34,772 --> 00:13:36,065
This is unbelievable.

202
00:13:36,732 --> 00:13:39,735
I'm starving.
Just wait until they get here.

203
00:13:40,861 --> 00:13:42,404
Why you…

204
00:13:42,488 --> 00:13:44,114
You scared me!

205
00:14:02,091 --> 00:14:03,092
What the…?

206
00:14:03,592 --> 00:14:07,555
"Mime artist, Jolly Pierrot."

207
00:14:11,225 --> 00:14:13,018
Jolly? You fucking bastard!

208
00:14:14,103 --> 00:14:15,062
Hey, Mime.

209
00:14:15,563 --> 00:14:17,481
Can't you speak Korean?

210
00:14:17,565 --> 00:14:20,192
If you're late,
you should damn well apologize first--

211
00:14:21,443 --> 00:14:22,361
Look at this.

212
00:14:26,782 --> 00:14:28,158
What the hell is this bastard?

213
00:14:28,242 --> 00:14:31,787
What is going on?
Your boss must be out of their mind.

214
00:14:31,871 --> 00:14:33,622
Who's the one with seniority here?

215
00:14:33,706 --> 00:14:36,584
Goddamn, you fucking…
We don't have time, so we're leaving,

216
00:14:36,667 --> 00:14:40,754
but if things go fucking south,
I'm going to rip you all to shreds!

217
00:14:40,838 --> 00:14:42,214
Got it?

218
00:14:42,798 --> 00:14:44,258
Hurry up and come out.

219
00:14:44,758 --> 00:14:47,469
Goddammit! I'm not gonna let you guys
put me out of a job.

220
00:15:02,985 --> 00:15:05,362
<i>There's only one thing you need to do,</i>
<i>Mr. Hyeok-jun.</i>

221
00:15:06,572 --> 00:15:12,202
Stay right next to the event specialist
until the end of your shift.

222
00:15:14,496 --> 00:15:18,751
<i>Leave the rest to the event specialist,</i>
<i>and they'll take care of everything.</i>

223
00:15:25,257 --> 00:15:29,053
PANG PANG EVENTS

224
00:15:39,939 --> 00:15:41,607
Fucking shit.

225
00:15:41,690 --> 00:15:44,735
I've got not one,
but two morons on my hands.

226
00:15:45,319 --> 00:15:47,863
When we get there, you guys better…

227
00:15:48,864 --> 00:15:50,991
SHINIL UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL
PROF. YOON

228
00:15:52,326 --> 00:15:54,912
Sir! Yes, sir!

229
00:15:54,995 --> 00:15:56,830
Yes, sir. I'm on my way.

230
00:15:57,790 --> 00:15:58,832
My apologies.

231
00:15:58,916 --> 00:16:00,834
I'll be there in a flash, sir!

232
00:16:01,335 --> 00:16:04,463
I promise the host
we hired especially for today

233
00:16:04,546 --> 00:16:06,799
will get the crowd going.

234
00:16:06,882 --> 00:16:10,094
You know you can count me in!
Yes, let's party all night, sir!

235
00:16:11,845 --> 00:16:14,014
Professor Yoon, I love you!

236
00:16:14,974 --> 00:16:15,891
Yes.

237
00:16:21,355 --> 00:16:23,482
These fucking bastards!

238
00:16:23,565 --> 00:16:27,111
Fuck! What's the damn problem?
I'm on my way, aren't I?

239
00:16:27,194 --> 00:16:29,989
Fuck! Those fucking bastards.

240
00:16:41,834 --> 00:16:43,293
Did you just laugh?

241
00:16:45,212 --> 00:16:47,631
You think me being
the damn doctor's lackey is funny?

242
00:16:47,715 --> 00:16:50,759
I mean, seriously.
You guys are unacceptable.

243
00:16:50,843 --> 00:16:53,971
I'm calling that damn boss of yours
and teaching you guys a lesson.

244
00:16:54,054 --> 00:16:55,097
Think this is funny?

245
00:16:57,224 --> 00:16:59,101
What the hell? Where'd it go?

246
00:17:04,231 --> 00:17:06,567
Are you nuts? Give it back.

247
00:17:06,650 --> 00:17:07,943
Give it back, damn it.

248
00:17:08,027 --> 00:17:09,278
Give it back. Hey!

249
00:17:09,361 --> 00:17:11,572
I'm going to call your damn boss.

250
00:17:12,239 --> 00:17:13,866
This guy's a fucking lunatic.

251
00:17:13,949 --> 00:17:16,285
Hey, part-timer, stop the car.
Stop it, you punk!

252
00:17:16,368 --> 00:17:17,953
Give it back, damn it.

253
00:17:18,037 --> 00:17:19,455
Give it!

254
00:17:20,497 --> 00:17:21,874
Give it back now, you bastard.

255
00:17:23,667 --> 00:17:24,710
Damn!

256
00:17:25,502 --> 00:17:26,628
Are you nuts?

257
00:17:29,298 --> 00:17:30,466
What's wrong with this thing?

258
00:17:34,178 --> 00:17:36,513
What's wrong with it? What's going on?

259
00:17:41,351 --> 00:17:42,478
Holy!

260
00:17:42,561 --> 00:17:44,563
Why's it doing this all of a sudden?

261
00:17:44,646 --> 00:17:46,315
What the hell are you doing?

262
00:17:46,398 --> 00:17:50,194
No, the car's moving on its own right now!

263
00:17:50,277 --> 00:17:52,279
Just stop the car!

264
00:17:55,074 --> 00:17:56,283
You crazy bastards!

265
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:04,708
Just stop the damn car!

266
00:18:08,545 --> 00:18:10,130
That's what I just saw!

267
00:18:10,214 --> 00:18:12,174
The rabbit!

268
00:18:41,203 --> 00:18:42,579
Rest stop.

269
00:18:43,997 --> 00:18:47,209
REST STOP

270
00:18:49,294 --> 00:18:52,214
Damn you. Get out.

271
00:18:53,382 --> 00:18:55,259
My phone.

272
00:18:55,759 --> 00:18:57,177
Get out, you bastard!

273
00:19:01,682 --> 00:19:04,059
Hey, you…

274
00:19:06,645 --> 00:19:10,107
So you do know who's in charge.

275
00:19:10,607 --> 00:19:11,817
Damn! I should just…

276
00:19:12,317 --> 00:19:15,988
What do you think you're doing,
pulling that crap with those cheap tricks?

277
00:19:16,989 --> 00:19:17,865
My phone.

278
00:19:18,365 --> 00:19:19,491
Where's my phone?

279
00:19:27,291 --> 00:19:28,625
Here's your phone.

280
00:19:28,709 --> 00:19:30,002
I can't believe this.

281
00:19:30,085 --> 00:19:32,045
How did it end up there?

282
00:19:32,129 --> 00:19:32,963
Hey, part-timer.

283
00:19:33,839 --> 00:19:36,800
Go throw that away
and get me some water from the store.

284
00:19:36,884 --> 00:19:38,010
Yes, sir.

285
00:19:38,594 --> 00:19:39,887
You're all dead meat today.

286
00:19:40,387 --> 00:19:41,722
They sent me these morons?

287
00:19:42,222 --> 00:19:43,891
Where's that number for Pang Pang?

288
00:19:54,860 --> 00:19:57,404
What are you waiting for? Go get me water.

289
00:19:58,030 --> 00:20:00,240
I think he should come with me--

290
00:20:00,324 --> 00:20:02,618
Just go get me water!

291
00:20:02,701 --> 00:20:04,703
Who needs two people to buy water?

292
00:20:05,204 --> 00:20:08,749
<i>Donning a red hat pulled down low</i>

293
00:20:08,832 --> 00:20:12,878
<i>I'm a pierrot who always carries a smile</i>

294
00:20:14,338 --> 00:20:18,133
<i>Behind my blue smile</i>

295
00:20:18,217 --> 00:20:21,303
<i>Lie tears nobody knows</i>

296
00:20:32,940 --> 00:20:35,776
You're hungry?

297
00:20:37,945 --> 00:20:39,279
Do you want some <i>gimbap</i>?

298
00:20:44,868 --> 00:20:45,869
GIMBAP

299
00:20:49,581 --> 00:20:51,500
We'll take these two.

300
00:20:52,668 --> 00:20:54,002
That'll be 5,000 won.

301
00:20:58,882 --> 00:21:01,218
- Thank you.
- Have a nice day.

302
00:21:09,017 --> 00:21:10,769
Wait, no. That's the wrapper.

303
00:21:38,839 --> 00:21:40,674
HEAD OF PANG PANG EVENT

304
00:21:40,757 --> 00:21:43,302
Guess the bastard now knows
he made a big mistake.

305
00:21:45,137 --> 00:21:49,725
Do you realize I'm going through
something really absurd right now?

306
00:21:49,808 --> 00:21:51,560
<i>Sorry? Where are you right now?</i>

307
00:21:51,643 --> 00:21:54,271
<i>My guys have been waiting</i>
<i>in your company lot for an hour,</i>

308
00:21:54,354 --> 00:21:56,023
<i>but you were unreachable.</i>

309
00:21:56,106 --> 00:21:57,190
What are you saying?

310
00:21:57,274 --> 00:22:00,819
I'm on my way to the venue
with the morons from your company.

311
00:22:01,361 --> 00:22:02,738
<i>You left for the venue?</i>

312
00:22:03,238 --> 00:22:04,573
<i>You must be mistaken.</i>

313
00:22:05,073 --> 00:22:07,409
<i>My employees are still in the parking lot.</i>

314
00:22:12,039 --> 00:22:13,457
Then who are those bastards?

315
00:22:20,255 --> 00:22:21,089
Hey!

316
00:22:21,673 --> 00:22:24,009
Who the hell are you guys?

317
00:22:24,551 --> 00:22:29,389
Pang Pang's boss just called.
His guys are still in the parking lot!

318
00:22:29,473 --> 00:22:30,307
What?

319
00:22:33,560 --> 00:22:35,687
We were sent from a staffing agency--

320
00:22:35,771 --> 00:22:36,813
Who are you, bastards?

321
00:22:37,939 --> 00:22:42,319
Are you assholes baiting people
for some streaming content or something?

322
00:22:42,402 --> 00:22:44,154
You son of a bitch!

323
00:22:45,155 --> 00:22:47,491
You're going to get sued big time.

324
00:22:48,033 --> 00:22:49,326
Give me the car keys now.

325
00:22:49,409 --> 00:22:51,161
Give me the damn keys!

326
00:23:03,590 --> 00:23:04,424
Crazy bastard.

327
00:23:08,428 --> 00:23:10,055
This bastard, seriously.

328
00:23:15,018 --> 00:23:15,977
Don't do it.

329
00:23:17,729 --> 00:23:19,106
You lunatic.

330
00:23:23,860 --> 00:23:24,694
Where'd they go?

331
00:23:25,195 --> 00:23:26,780
So you want to go all the way, huh?

332
00:23:27,656 --> 00:23:29,491
What? Why's it getting longer?

333
00:23:29,574 --> 00:23:30,826
What the hell?

334
00:23:45,173 --> 00:23:46,299
No, don't…

335
00:23:46,800 --> 00:23:48,885
Wait, is that it?

336
00:23:49,970 --> 00:23:51,138
What are you doing?

337
00:23:51,763 --> 00:23:52,597
Don't do that.

338
00:23:52,681 --> 00:23:54,808
Got them! Wait a second.

339
00:23:57,227 --> 00:23:58,937
Shit! Hey, get me out of here!

340
00:24:00,188 --> 00:24:01,481
You son of a--

341
00:24:04,359 --> 00:24:05,694
Your body…

342
00:24:06,194 --> 00:24:07,529
I can't breathe!

343
00:24:34,181 --> 00:24:35,223
What's wrong with this?

344
00:24:36,141 --> 00:24:39,936
<i>Stay right next to the event specialist</i>
<i>until the end of your shift.</i>

345
00:24:40,020 --> 00:24:40,896
EMERGENCY

346
00:24:54,576 --> 00:24:55,410
Fuck.

347
00:25:07,297 --> 00:25:08,965
Stay away!

348
00:25:16,431 --> 00:25:17,724
What's wrong with this?

349
00:25:24,898 --> 00:25:26,775
Don't come near me.

350
00:25:31,446 --> 00:25:33,198
Don't come near me!

351
00:25:44,417 --> 00:25:46,670
What's wrong with my arm?

352
00:25:54,094 --> 00:25:56,012
What's wrong with this?

353
00:26:06,398 --> 00:26:08,608
I'm just a part-timer.

354
00:26:09,109 --> 00:26:12,279
I'm at the bottom.
Like top, middle, bottom. The bottom.

355
00:26:14,364 --> 00:26:18,034
If you let me live, I'll do anything.

356
00:26:18,535 --> 00:26:20,412
I'll do anything you tell me to do.

357
00:26:20,495 --> 00:26:23,290
Shit, I can't fucking die!

358
00:26:23,373 --> 00:26:27,502
I have to work and pay my mom back. Fuck.

359
00:26:29,045 --> 00:26:31,840
Please spare me just this once.

360
00:26:32,340 --> 00:26:33,300
Just this once.

361
00:26:45,478 --> 00:26:46,855
You want me to choose?

362
00:27:35,904 --> 00:27:38,198
<i>Starting route guidance.</i>

363
00:28:12,732 --> 00:28:13,566
Hello?

364
00:28:13,650 --> 00:28:17,696
<i>Jo Jun-seop, you son of a bitch!</i>
<i>How many damn times do I have to call you?</i>

365
00:28:17,779 --> 00:28:19,239
<i>Where are you right now?</i>

366
00:28:19,739 --> 00:28:20,990
<i>Where the hell are you?</i>

367
00:28:21,074 --> 00:28:22,575
I'm really sorry,

368
00:28:22,659 --> 00:28:25,286
but we got into an accident on the way.

369
00:28:25,370 --> 00:28:26,788
The person in charge is--

370
00:28:27,372 --> 00:28:29,958
<i>Goddammit. Are you fucking making excuses?</i>

371
00:28:30,458 --> 00:28:31,835
<i>Everyone's waiting right now.</i>

372
00:28:31,918 --> 00:28:34,879
<i>So you got into an accident.</i>
<i>But did you die or something?</i>

373
00:28:34,963 --> 00:28:38,800
<i>You're supposed to show up,</i>
<i>even if you have to crawl here or die!</i>

374
00:28:39,300 --> 00:28:40,552
<i>Is our money a joke to you?</i>

375
00:28:43,012 --> 00:28:44,013
<i>Hey!</i>

376
00:28:44,514 --> 00:28:46,933
<i>Do your goddamn job!</i>

377
00:28:47,976 --> 00:28:51,312
<i>If things get canceled today</i>
<i>because of you, I'll really kill you.</i>

378
00:28:52,772 --> 00:28:53,982
<i>Fucking hell!</i>

379
00:28:54,482 --> 00:28:58,445
<i>They should stop inferior trash like you</i>
<i>from reproducing by law.</i>

380
00:28:59,154 --> 00:29:00,155
<i>Damn it!</i>

381
00:29:03,032 --> 00:29:03,867
SHINIL HOSPITAL
PROF. YOON

382
00:29:11,916 --> 00:29:12,792
You're telling me…

383
00:29:15,837 --> 00:29:17,088
to get to work, right?

384
00:29:26,473 --> 00:29:30,435
SHINIL UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL OFFSITE
SPONSORED BY KD PHARMACEUTICAL

385
00:29:35,857 --> 00:29:37,275
You damn shit.

386
00:29:39,444 --> 00:29:40,361
Get on my eye level.

387
00:29:40,445 --> 00:29:41,654
I'm sorry.

388
00:29:43,239 --> 00:29:44,783
Where's that bastard Jo Jun-seop?

389
00:29:46,785 --> 00:29:51,581
Mr. Jo suddenly felt unwell,
so he went home--

390
00:29:51,664 --> 00:29:53,041
You piece of shit.

391
00:29:54,083 --> 00:29:57,879
Tell that son of a bitch
that he's done for in this industry.

392
00:29:58,379 --> 00:30:01,174
Yes. I'll tell him.

393
00:30:01,257 --> 00:30:04,219
Man, these inferior sons of bitches.

394
00:30:35,458 --> 00:30:38,127
That fucking idiot.

395
00:30:38,753 --> 00:30:39,587
Hurry up.

396
00:30:40,296 --> 00:30:41,965
Hurry up and start, damn it!

397
00:30:44,300 --> 00:30:47,971
Yes, hello. Today's event…

398
00:30:48,555 --> 00:30:50,348
Many of you…

399
00:30:50,849 --> 00:30:52,976
We came, arrived late today, so…

400
00:30:59,566 --> 00:31:03,945
Let me introduce the mime artist,
Jolly Pierrot…

401
00:31:26,175 --> 00:31:27,218
Ten o'clock?

402
00:31:27,343 --> 00:31:28,386
PART-TIME JOB COMPLETED
6,018,000 WON

403
00:32:04,088 --> 00:32:07,675
Why spoil this happy vibe
with such creepy makeup?

404
00:32:15,183 --> 00:32:16,267
What the hell?

405
00:32:16,351 --> 00:32:17,894
Who are you?

406
00:32:17,977 --> 00:32:19,103
What are you doing?

407
00:32:34,953 --> 00:32:35,954
No.

408
00:32:36,996 --> 00:32:38,081
This is all fake.

409
00:32:43,252 --> 00:32:47,757
<i>I'd rather be a pierrot</i>

410
00:32:47,840 --> 00:32:51,302
<i>Who smiles</i>

411
00:32:51,970 --> 00:32:56,516
<i>I'd rather be a pierrot</i>

412
00:32:56,599 --> 00:32:59,435
<i>Who knows sadness</i>

413
00:33:00,645 --> 00:33:05,066
<i>I'd rather be a pierrot</i>

414
00:33:05,566 --> 00:33:08,611
<i>Who smiles</i>

415
00:33:09,362 --> 00:33:13,950
<i>I'd rather be a pierrot</i>

416
00:33:14,033 --> 00:33:17,662
<i>Who knows sadness</i>

417
00:33:18,371 --> 00:33:21,290
<i>I'd rather be a pierrot</i>

418
00:33:30,550 --> 00:33:35,054
Help me…

419
00:33:39,350 --> 00:33:40,309
No.

420
00:33:42,729 --> 00:33:44,897
There's no way this is real.

421
00:33:46,858 --> 00:33:52,697
I'm sorry…

422
